Have you ever felt stuck in life or don't feel like doing stuff because you're afraid what other people might think of you?

But let me tell you 2 things I learned this year about taking risks and how can you implement those things in your life as well

# Your Actions don't have to align with your thoughts/feelings

![](/images/posts/how-to-achieve-anything-in-life/Pasted%20image%2020260709160906.png)

I learned this lesson in one of Ali Abdaal's videos that your actions don't have to be dependent on what you're feeling. So what does that mean?

Nobody wants to go to the school by waking up early in the morning, do we? We feel tired, sleepy and exhausted. But we still leave our bed, get ready and go to the school

So see? We were feeling like not doing the task but we still took actions towards doing it.

So the way I like to implement this technique in my day to day life is, whenever I am feeling like not doing something, like not publishing reels on my Instagram account because I am afraid of what my friends and family might think of me. I immediately take out my journal and make 2 columns. One for **Feelings** and one for **Actions**.

In the feelings section I write whatever negative thought or feelings that are running through my mind and in the actions section I write what action I had to take.

![](/images/posts/how-to-achieve-anything-in-life/Drawing%202026-07-07%2000.16.33.excalidraw.png)

So this way I can clearly see what is in front of me, what I have to do so a lot of my brain fog clears out and I start to see clearly.

# People **will** have opinions about you

We usually listen online that you can do whatever you want because it's just you who is thinking that what others might think of you, or something about the spotlight effect

That is true for most of the part but in Pakistan people are what we call **velay**, meaning they don't have anything to do so they start to talk about others and start calling them out

So people will definitely have opinions about you!

But you don't have to worry about them, you just have to keep their opinions aside just keep doing whatever you're doing as long as it makes you happy

Just keep in mind that they are having opinions about you because you're doing something that you're passionate about and they're jealous of you seeing you work so hard for your dream and they are just the spectators in your amazing journey

So go ahead and achieve that dream of yours.

I am rooting for you 🚀
